    "temporalRange": "Kimmeridgian, 154–152 Ma",
    "diet": "herbivore",
    "locomotionType": "",
    "description": "Laosaurus (meaning \"stone or fossil lizard\") is a genus of neornithischian dinosaur. The type species, Laosaurus celer, was first described by O.C. Marsh in 1878 from remains from the Oxfordian-Tithonian-age Upper Jurassic Morrison Formation of Wyoming. The validity of this genus is doubtful because it is based on fragmentary fossils. A second species from the Morrison Formation, L. gracilis, and a species from the late Cretaceous Allison Formation of Alberta, Canada, Laosaurus minimus, are also considered dubious.",
