      "title": "Migmanychion",
      "description": "Migmanychion is a genus of small-bodied theropod dinosaur from the Early Cretaceous of China. It is known from a well-articulated left hand, which gives it its name, showing a peculiar combination of features shared with therizinosauroids and oviraptorosaurs. Migmanychion is a maniraptoran theropod, but its precise placement within the clade is unclear. It seems most closely related to Fukuivenator, which is currently thought to be a basal therizinosaur. Migmanychion was roughly 2 m in length.",
