    "id": 718,
    "name": "Nanshiungosaurus",
    "temporalRange": "Late Cretaceous, ~67–66 Ma",
    "diet": "carnivore",
    "locomotionType": "biped",
    "description": "Nanshiungosaurus (meaning \"Nanxiong's lizard\") is a genus of therizinosaurid that lived in what is now Asia during the Late Cretaceous of South China. The type species, Nanshiungosaurus brevispinus, was first discovered in 1974 and described in 1979 by Dong Zhiming. It is represented by a single specimen preserving most of the cervical and dorsal vertebrae with the pelvis. A supposed and unlikely second species, \"Nanshiungosaurus\" bohlini, was found in 1992 and described in 1997. It is also represented by vertebrae but this species however, differs in geological age and lacks authentic characteristics compared to the type, making its affinity to the genus unsupported.",
