      "title": "Oblitosaurus",
      "description": "Oblitosaurus is a genus of ornithopod dinosaur from the Late Jurassic of Spain. Like other ornithopods, it had a short neck and a beak which it used to feed on plants. The thumb claw of Oblitosaurus was adapted into a small conical spur, and it could likely walk quadrupedally or bipedally. It could reach around 7 m in length, making it the largest known European ornithopod of the Jurassic.",
