    "description": "Paraxenisaurus (, meaning \"strange lizard\") is an extinct genus of ornithomimosaurian theropod from the Late Cretaceous Cerro del Pueblo Formation of Coahuila in Mexico.  The genus contains a single species, P. normalensis, which is known from a few bones of tail, hips, hands, and feet.  The specific epithet was given in honor of the Benemérita Normal School of Coahuila, a teacher training institution, where the fossils were reposited.  It is a member of the family Deinocheiridae and is the only member of that clade known from Laramidia.",
