    "diet": "herbivore",
    "locomotionType": "quadruped",
    "description": "Tambatitanis (meaning \"Tamba giant\", after Tamba, the name given to the northwest of Kansai, Japan[1]) is an extinct genus of titanosauriform dinosaur from the Early Cretaceous (probably early Albian[2]) of Japan. It is known from a single type species, Tambatitanis amicitiae, which is known from the Sasayama Group.[1] It was probably around 14 m (46 ft) long and its mass was estimated at some 4 tonnes (3.9 long tons; 4.4 short tons).[2] It was a basal titanosauriform and possibly belonged to the Euhelopodidae.[1] The holotype was collected between 2006 and 2010.[3]",
