    "description": "Eucercosaurus (meaning \"good-tailed lizard\"[1]) is the name given to a genus of ornithopod dinosaur from the Albian stage of the Early Cretaceous. It was an ornithopod discovered in the Cambridge Greensand of England and is known from 19 centra, 3 sacrals, 4 dorsals and 12 caudals, and a neural arch found near Trumpington, Cambridgeshire.[1][2] The type species, E. tanyspondylus, was described by British paleontologist Harry Seeley in 1879.[3]",
